  ],
  "text": "The blue whale's ancestor was a deer sized animal that hunted on riverbanks. Whales cannot breathe underwater. That was always the clue. Fifty million years ago, one of them started spending more time in the shallows. The legs got shorter. The nostrils crept up the skull. The fossils come in order. Each one a little more whale than the last. And the change never finished. The leftovers are still in there. A whale still has hip bones. Floating loose, attached to nothing at all. And inside every flipper there are finger bones. Five of them. The largest animal alive is still carrying the hands it once walked on. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
